Scope and why MIT: the MIT licence covers the source code in this repository
(packages/core, apps/web, apps/mobile, services/api, scripts, tests, e2e). It is
short, permissive and widely understood, so the project can be continued,
hosted or handed to another developer without legal friction.

Not covered by this licence:
- packages/content (the reading passages and questions): original works licensed
  separately under CC BY 4.0 — see packages/content/LICENSE.
- spec-source/ (the original specification pack and hand-off documents): included
  unchanged for traceability; rights remain with their authors.
- Third-party dependencies: under their own licences (see package-lock.json and
  services/api/requirements.txt).
